{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwfQy2cMW2acuuca7Y5K","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dashboard and the alert rule both exist, and the rule is enabled. I haven't opened the dashboard or confirmed that the rule's query matches any documents.\n\n**What the data holds:** Each document is a web request, with a `timestamp`, a `response` code, `bytes`, a file `extension`, `geo.src` and `geo.dest` countries, and details of the client and machine. `response` is a text field, so I filter on `response.keyword`.\n\n**Dashboard:** \"EFF-846935be Web logs overview\" has five panels:\n- Total requests\n- Requests over time\n- Responses by status code\n- Top source countries\n- Average bytes by extension\n\nIt's at http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-846935be-web-logs-overview-8aa8176d1815.\n\n**Rule:** \"EFF-846935be 5xx spike\" is an Elasticsearch query rule that runs every minute. It fires when more than 10 requests with a `response.keyword` starting with \"5\" arrive within 5 minutes.\n\nThe rule has no actions attached, because no connectors are configured. It will register alerts in Kibana but won't send notifications anywhere."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":157,"cache_read_input_tokens":20278,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":157},"output_tokens":381,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4eb1cb7-866c-5bbf-8d81-a8d5acd83be3","uuid":"fa73dfea-6bb7-4354-b812-4dfddc58644b","timestamp":"2026-10-12T03:51:16.183Z","request_id":"req_011CfwfQxoDYpG3RZ5mQXAa7"}
